    "# \"\"\"\n",
    "# build_cache.py -- decode every mugshot ONCE, resize, and store a uint8 NHWC .npy memmap.\n",
    "#\n",
    "# After this one-off pass training reads raw uint8 bytes from page cache and does all augmentation on the GPU.\n",
    "#\n",
    "#   python build_cache.py --base_dir <.../idoc-mugshots> --cache_dir /kaggle/working/cache --size 224\n",
    "#\n",
    "# Speed (the first version took 63 min = 19 img/s on Kaggle, i.e. ~200 ms per image per worker -> latency/IO and\n",
    "# full-resolution-decode bound):\n",
    "#   * a THREAD pool (default 24) instead of 4 processes: cv2.imread releases the GIL, so file reads overlap\n",
    "#     each other and the 4 cores stay busy decoding\n",
    "#   * JPEG decode-time downscaling (--reduce auto): picks the largest 1/2, 1/4 or 1/8 DCT downscale that still\n",
    "#     leaves >= --size pixels on the short side, then the same INTER_AREA resize as before (--reduce 1 = old behaviour)\n",
