    "## Interpretability: how does the trained model decide, and where does it look?\n",
    "Run this on the **already trained** model; it needs one GPU and takes roughly 10\u201315 minutes (not measured). **Every input is passed explicitly on the command line** (the cell below shows them): the labels CSV, the image cache, the split file and the checkpoint written by `train.py`, so nothing is re-trained or hard-wired. `train.py` gained a `pretrained=` argument for this, so **re-run the `%%writefile train.py` cell first**; `labels.py` and `report.py` must also be in the working folder.\n",
