    "* **Gallery** (`gallery_<category>.png`): confident true positives and false alarms with Grad-CAM next to **occlusion sensitivity** (slide a grey window, measure the logit drop; slower but model-agnostic). If the two disagree, trust neither much.\n",
    "* **Region ablation** (`region_ablation.csv`): AUC with parts of the image removed. Read the results in **pairs**: *face only* high means the face is sufficient; *face blanked* low means it is necessary. *Head blanked (background + body only)* staying high means the signal lives in the surroundings (clothing, background, placards, camera). Grey fill is out-of-distribution, so compare the rows with each other rather than reading absolute AUCs. Colour, blur, low-res, shuffled patches and upside-down test what kind of information is used.\n",
